WEBVTT

00:51.384 --> 00:53.344
MAMAMON

00:54.679 --> 00:56.014
Mom?

00:56.765 --> 00:59.434
Finally, you picked up!

01:01.352 --> 01:04.064
I don't hear from you at all lately!

01:04.147 --> 01:07.025
How is your move going?

01:09.819 --> 01:12.155
I'm working on it…

01:12.238 --> 01:16.159
Also, you don't need to come and help me
this time.

01:17.535 --> 01:20.163
You don't need me to go?

01:21.706 --> 01:24.793
Yeah. It's so sudden, anyway.

01:25.668 --> 01:27.545
I have school too, so…

01:27.629 --> 01:30.924
How can you move all by yourself!

01:31.925 --> 01:33.259
I'm really okay.

01:33.343 --> 01:35.178
I'll try to do what I can on my own.

01:43.937 --> 01:46.397
Your application was accepted.

01:50.485 --> 01:52.445
Thank you.

01:52.529 --> 01:55.281
I will get all the contracts ready
as fast as I can.

01:55.365 --> 01:56.199
Okay.

02:00.870 --> 02:02.163
I GOT THE APARTMENT

02:02.247 --> 02:03.957
YAY

02:05.583 --> 02:08.211
KAEDE REAL ESTATE

02:12.048 --> 02:13.133
I HOPE I CAN SIGN THE CONTRACT ON MY OWN.

02:13.216 --> 02:14.050
I'M NERVOUS. I SIGNED IT!

02:14.634 --> 02:16.469
Is he not on lunch break yet?

02:20.557 --> 02:22.058
RIN

02:33.695 --> 02:34.529
Taiga.

02:35.655 --> 02:37.323
You should take a break when you can too.

02:37.407 --> 02:38.366
Okay.

02:40.785 --> 02:41.828
Shige.

02:42.704 --> 02:44.622
How were this week's appetizers?

02:45.915 --> 02:47.041
They were good.

02:49.669 --> 02:51.713
I'll leave the appetizers
to you from now on.

02:53.006 --> 02:55.008
- Okay! I'll do my best.
- Good.

02:55.091 --> 02:55.925
TANOMI

03:00.638 --> 03:02.140
All right…

03:05.018 --> 03:05.852
RIN

03:07.604 --> 03:08.813
‪RIN

03:08.897 --> 03:10.106
I'M NERVOUS.

03:10.189 --> 03:11.274
I SIGNED IT!

04:18.967 --> 04:21.719
Communication issues, huh?

04:25.598 --> 04:28.559
You'd better solve that
as soon as you can.

04:31.104 --> 04:34.023
This isn't the first time, right?

04:34.107 --> 04:36.901
Why are you ignoring the problem?

04:38.820 --> 04:41.155
If we take the time
to get to know each other,

04:41.990 --> 04:43.783
won't these issues solve themselves?

04:44.284 --> 04:45.368
Park Rin.

04:45.451 --> 04:49.414
Are you going to eat the onigiri
one grain of rice at a time?

04:49.497 --> 04:50.873
At this rate,

04:50.957 --> 04:54.794
you'll never find out
what the stuffing is.

04:55.378 --> 04:59.215
But we just started dating.

04:59.299 --> 05:01.426
If you're dating,

05:01.509 --> 05:04.304
then stop stressing about it
all on your own,

05:04.387 --> 05:07.015
and sink your teeth into Onigiri Man!

05:09.851 --> 05:10.852
Okay?

05:23.781 --> 05:24.782
TANOMI

05:24.866 --> 05:27.827
And ketchup for the pork chops.

05:27.910 --> 05:30.371
- Okay.
- Here is the shopping list.

05:30.455 --> 05:31.497
- Okay.
- Thanks.

05:32.498 --> 05:33.583
Good evening.

05:35.918 --> 05:38.171
Hey, Rin. Good to see you.

05:38.254 --> 05:39.255
Welcome.

05:40.381 --> 05:43.342
All right, then. Maybe I'll go home.

05:44.135 --> 05:46.179
- I'll leave the rest to you.
- Okay. Good bye.

05:46.262 --> 05:47.305
Bye.

05:49.599 --> 05:50.641
Annyeong.

05:57.899 --> 05:59.358
Sorry for showing up so suddenly.

06:01.360 --> 06:02.320
Just give me a second.

06:02.403 --> 06:04.405
I'll be done soon. Come in.

06:15.208 --> 06:17.418
I got my apartment.

06:18.753 --> 06:22.548
What? That's great! Which one?

06:23.758 --> 06:27.261
The last place we toured.

06:31.474 --> 06:36.187
This place, huh?
That's great. Congratulations.

06:37.814 --> 06:39.023
Thanks.

06:40.817 --> 06:41.776
Wow…

06:44.112 --> 06:45.196
What?

06:45.780 --> 06:47.240
It's almost your birthday.

06:49.826 --> 06:51.160
Yeah, it is.

06:55.206 --> 06:58.292
I'll ask Shige if I can take that day off.

06:58.376 --> 07:00.169
What? Really?

07:01.379 --> 07:02.505
Let me celebrate it.

07:03.840 --> 07:05.133
I'd love that.

07:05.216 --> 07:08.803
But first, we have to celebrate
your new place.

07:09.303 --> 07:10.596
Here it is.

07:12.223 --> 07:13.182
How cute.

07:14.350 --> 07:15.893
RAMEN - OPEN

07:15.977 --> 07:17.437
What a cool place.

07:17.520 --> 07:19.230
You've never been to a ramen stand?

07:20.523 --> 07:22.400
But I've seen them in anime.

07:23.568 --> 07:24.694
Welcome.

07:24.777 --> 07:25.736
Let's sit down.

07:26.737 --> 07:28.906
- For two, please.
- Two? Okay, have a seat.

07:30.825 --> 07:32.952
- Two ramen and…
- Two ramen.

07:33.619 --> 07:34.620
What do you want to drink?

07:35.496 --> 07:37.039
I'll have a highball.

07:37.123 --> 07:38.374
Two highballs please.

07:38.458 --> 07:40.793
- Two highballs. Okay.
- Thank you.

07:48.759 --> 07:50.470
Thanks for waiting. Here's your highball.

07:51.554 --> 07:52.847
Thank you.

07:56.267 --> 07:57.727
Well then, cheers.

07:58.227 --> 07:59.896
Cheers.

08:06.736 --> 08:10.031
My photo of this stand is getting likes.

08:10.948 --> 08:14.243
Social media?
Do you upload a lot of photos?

08:15.661 --> 08:17.663
Things like food and doodles.

08:19.165 --> 08:21.751
Did you draw that?

08:23.669 --> 08:25.379
These are by an artist that I love.

08:26.172 --> 08:28.341
Every piece is so unique.

08:28.424 --> 08:29.759
I've been a long-time fan.

08:31.260 --> 08:32.637
I see.

08:39.560 --> 08:40.645
Anything else?

08:41.646 --> 08:42.939
Do you want to ask me anything?

08:44.524 --> 08:45.733
What?

08:47.902 --> 08:51.113
I want you to get to know me better.

08:51.781 --> 08:55.660
And I want to get to know you better too.

08:57.954 --> 08:59.956
Did something happen?

09:03.334 --> 09:07.046
Taiga, are you not that good
at keeping in touch?

09:13.427 --> 09:16.097
When you don't read my messages,

09:16.180 --> 09:18.099
or a day goes by without a word from you,

09:18.599 --> 09:21.102
I start to wonder
if you have no interest in me.

09:23.104 --> 09:24.021
I get worried.

09:32.446 --> 09:34.865
Thanks for waiting. Here is your ramen.

09:34.949 --> 09:36.534
NOODLE HOUSE MIYABI

09:36.617 --> 09:38.619
Enjoy. Thanks for waiting.

09:38.703 --> 09:40.538
- Here is your ramen.
- Thank you.

09:45.167 --> 09:46.168
I'm sorry.

09:46.961 --> 09:51.841
From now on,
I promise I'll contact you once a day.

09:55.344 --> 09:57.722
Just once a day?

10:00.141 --> 10:01.809
I didn't mean that literally.

10:02.685 --> 10:05.104
What I mean is, I'll work on it.

10:10.985 --> 10:12.236
Thank you.

10:14.322 --> 10:15.865
Let's eat.

10:22.330 --> 10:23.706
- Thank you.
- Enjoy.

10:29.378 --> 10:30.463
It's delicious.

10:36.552 --> 10:37.928
Yeah, that's it.

10:41.599 --> 10:42.850
Did you find it?

10:44.685 --> 10:45.853
Thank goodness.

10:46.437 --> 10:48.648
Can you hold onto it until the night?

10:49.815 --> 10:50.775
Okay.

10:50.858 --> 10:53.110
Bye. Oh, wait.

10:55.071 --> 10:58.032
Sorry, this might be really random, but…

10:58.115 --> 11:00.159
What? What is it?

11:00.701 --> 11:02.161
What kind of gift

11:03.245 --> 11:04.872
would make you happy?

11:05.456 --> 11:06.290
Huh?

11:06.374 --> 11:09.794
Well, it's almost Rin's birthday.

11:10.795 --> 11:12.713
I was thinking about what to get,

11:13.255 --> 11:16.092
but nothing really stood out.

11:19.220 --> 11:21.013
Birthday, huh?

11:23.307 --> 11:26.352
There's no point
if someone tells you what to get.

11:27.061 --> 11:31.440
Wouldn't she be happy to get something
that comes from your heart?

11:31.941 --> 11:33.234
- You think so?
- Yeah.

11:34.944 --> 11:35.903
Well…

11:35.986 --> 11:38.406
The beginning stages of dating
are always fun.

11:38.906 --> 11:39.990
So take your time and think.

11:41.242 --> 11:44.286
I'll do that. Thanks. Bye.

11:50.084 --> 11:51.127
Mom.

11:52.211 --> 11:53.963
Mom, wake up.

11:54.046 --> 11:57.883
- Noa?
- Drink water.

11:59.176 --> 12:01.137
BIRTHDAY GIFTS FOR YOUR GIRLFRIEND

12:01.220 --> 12:03.222
TOP 20 GIFTS
THAT YOUR GIRLFRIEND WOULD LOVE

12:18.863 --> 12:20.865
LOOK

12:20.948 --> 12:23.492
RAMEN

12:54.064 --> 12:56.066
- Excuse me.
- Yes?

12:56.150 --> 12:57.860
Do you have this?

12:59.069 --> 13:02.281
We don't carry that. I'm sorry.

13:02.364 --> 13:03.324
I see.

13:03.908 --> 13:05.409
Excuse me.

13:06.285 --> 13:08.537
I'm looking for this book.

13:09.246 --> 13:12.416
I guess it's out-of-print,
and I can't find it anywhere.

13:24.970 --> 13:26.388
All right.

13:36.774 --> 13:40.027
- It's eomma…
- You don't need to answer it?

13:40.611 --> 13:44.615
It's okay. It'll be a nightmare
if she finds out you're here.

13:44.698 --> 13:46.200
I'll call her back later.

13:51.455 --> 13:52.498
Taiga.

13:53.415 --> 13:56.085
Can I move your stuff over there?

13:56.794 --> 13:57.962
I'll do it!

14:10.641 --> 14:12.977
Helping her move, huh?

14:14.186 --> 14:17.147
Taiga is so the type
to pamper his girlfriend.

14:19.900 --> 14:22.528
Not like some boyfriends out there
who do slots on pay day.

14:22.611 --> 14:23.445
Here.

14:23.529 --> 14:24.947
- Have some oshinko.
- Thanks.

14:25.614 --> 14:26.740
Welcome.

14:30.494 --> 14:31.954
Go ahead and have a seat.

14:36.375 --> 14:39.712
Please sit.

14:47.261 --> 14:48.387
What is he saying?

14:48.470 --> 14:50.764
He's asking if there's an English menu.

14:50.848 --> 14:52.016
We don't have that.

14:52.099 --> 14:53.684
Of course we don't.

14:55.269 --> 14:56.854
He's saying something…

15:13.537 --> 15:14.538
Delicious.

15:18.667 --> 15:20.085
Good, good…

15:24.590 --> 15:26.008
Thanks.

15:28.093 --> 15:30.179
Should I make an English menu
or something?

15:31.096 --> 15:32.681
That's true…

15:32.765 --> 15:36.435
We get a lot of foreign customers lately,
so that would be great.

15:40.022 --> 15:42.232
But don't expect too much.

15:42.316 --> 15:44.652
- Of course I have high expectations.
- Don't.

15:44.735 --> 15:46.320
In addition to English,

15:47.237 --> 15:48.280
we need French,

15:48.364 --> 15:51.241
- Italian, Spanish, Korean…
- No, no!

15:55.663 --> 15:57.206
It's done!

15:58.958 --> 16:01.043
Good work. Here.

16:01.126 --> 16:02.461
Thank you.

16:07.675 --> 16:11.387
This is my first time moving on my own.

16:11.971 --> 16:14.556
So having you with me was very reassuring.

16:48.882 --> 16:50.718
Hello, who's there?

17:01.854 --> 17:03.272
Mom?!

17:03.355 --> 17:05.649
Rin, it's your birthday tomorrow, right?

17:05.733 --> 17:08.694
So I came here to see you.
Hurry up and open the door!

17:09.862 --> 17:11.488
Give me a second.

17:12.740 --> 17:14.491
My mom is here! What should I do?

17:14.575 --> 17:17.953
- What?
- What should I do…

17:18.037 --> 17:19.288
- Rin?
- Oh no…

17:21.540 --> 17:22.791
This way.

17:25.961 --> 17:28.213
I missed you, Rin!

17:29.256 --> 17:31.300
Good to see you, Mom.

17:31.383 --> 17:33.343
I missed you so much.

17:38.015 --> 17:42.061
You pretty much got everything organized.

17:42.144 --> 17:45.230
I booked a hotel,
because I thought it would be a mess.

17:45.939 --> 17:48.233
But at this rate,
I can stay here from tonight.

17:48.776 --> 17:52.571
Rin, where's your bedroom? That way?

17:52.654 --> 17:57.076
Mom! Mom!

17:58.285 --> 18:02.706
What a nice room. It's so fluffy.

18:02.790 --> 18:05.459
Rin, where's your extra futon?

18:06.668 --> 18:07.669
Over here?

18:09.379 --> 18:12.049
- Mom!
- What?

18:19.431 --> 18:22.518
I'm so hungry…

18:22.601 --> 18:26.522
Oh, you were hungry? Let's eat then!

18:28.524 --> 18:29.566
But you know,

18:30.234 --> 18:31.819
I'm so glad.

18:31.902 --> 18:33.529
I was worried

18:33.612 --> 18:37.574
that you had found
a boyfriend or something.

18:37.658 --> 18:39.451
I'm so relieved.

18:45.124 --> 18:46.291
I'm sorry.

18:53.173 --> 18:55.676
I put in extra sesame oil,
just how you like it.

19:12.192 --> 19:13.527
It smells good.

19:17.156 --> 19:18.782
She's in the bathroom, so go now.

19:18.866 --> 19:19.783
Huh?

19:20.826 --> 19:23.829
H… Hey… wait…

19:23.912 --> 19:25.747
Should we be sneaking around like this?

19:25.831 --> 19:28.250
Shouldn't I introduce myself properly?

19:28.333 --> 19:30.169
Are you crazy?

19:30.878 --> 19:33.046
Please, leave.

19:33.547 --> 19:35.215
What about your birthday?

19:35.299 --> 19:38.635
That… I want to spend with you
no matter what.

19:38.719 --> 19:40.596
I'll contact you as soon as she leaves.

19:40.679 --> 19:41.680
I promise.

19:42.973 --> 19:44.349
She's coming out! Hurry!

19:44.433 --> 19:45.934
Shoes, shoes, shoes!

20:07.414 --> 20:09.416
You like this, right?

20:10.626 --> 20:13.212
Here, eat the omelet too.

20:14.963 --> 20:16.048
How is school?

20:18.842 --> 20:21.595
Are you enjoying school?

20:23.472 --> 20:27.476
Are you studying like you should be?

20:28.143 --> 20:30.437
There's someone in my class
who's really good.

20:31.063 --> 20:35.234
And that person is inspiring me.

20:38.111 --> 20:42.699
Sometimes I wonder if I have any talent,
and get a little discouraged, though.

20:45.035 --> 20:46.620
But I just have to do my best!

20:50.040 --> 20:54.378
I guess the road to becoming
a creator is a tough one…

21:18.318 --> 21:20.404
Shige? Is something wrong?

21:20.487 --> 21:21.738
So, so, so sorry.

21:21.822 --> 21:24.992
I completely forgot that we had
a reservation for a big group.

21:26.076 --> 21:28.620
Can I ask you to come in,
just for two hours?

21:29.288 --> 21:31.206
What? Now?

21:31.290 --> 21:32.332
Excuse me.

21:32.416 --> 21:33.750
Yes, one moment please.

21:36.628 --> 21:39.089
I think I can come in.

21:39.172 --> 21:42.092
Really? You're a lifesaver. Hurry, please.

21:44.136 --> 21:45.137
Okay.

22:10.996 --> 22:12.164
Noa.

22:14.374 --> 22:17.627
- I haven't gotten paid yet, so no.
- Are you serious?

22:24.801 --> 22:26.094
What is that? English?

22:26.178 --> 22:27.345
Are you traveling?

22:28.305 --> 22:31.016
Not traveling, but…

22:31.099 --> 22:35.145
Vegas would be awesome.
The land of the free.

22:36.980 --> 22:40.859
But I'd be happy to go anywhere,
as long as I'm with you.

22:44.362 --> 22:48.366
But in order to do that,
we need to win first.

22:51.369 --> 22:52.746
Just one, okay?

22:52.829 --> 22:53.830
- Really?
- Yes.

23:00.253 --> 23:01.129
Paw.

23:02.672 --> 23:04.007
- Aren't you going to bark?
- Woof!

23:06.593 --> 23:08.720
You're the best girlfriend!

23:08.804 --> 23:10.180
All right, all right.

23:10.263 --> 23:11.932
- Can I go?
- Sure.

23:12.015 --> 23:14.726
- I will win, I promise.
- Yeah, yeah…

23:14.810 --> 23:15.727
Bye!

23:24.611 --> 23:26.780
That was delicious.

23:30.784 --> 23:32.244
I'm sorry, Mom.

23:33.870 --> 23:36.373
I'm really happy that you're here,

23:36.456 --> 23:40.544
but I still haven't finished my assignment
that's due today…

23:40.627 --> 23:42.838
Really?

23:43.463 --> 23:47.592
My goodness,
you should've told me that earlier.

23:47.676 --> 23:52.389
After I clean this all up,
I'll go back to my hotel.

23:52.472 --> 23:54.558
You don't have to worry about me.

23:54.641 --> 23:58.728
You work hard on your assignment! Okay?

24:09.447 --> 24:10.907
I'm so sorry, Mom.

24:12.450 --> 24:14.202
Thank you for waiting.

24:14.286 --> 24:16.246
- Here's your karaage.
- Can you take our order?

24:16.329 --> 24:18.498
- Yes.
- The seasonal carpaccio please.

24:18.582 --> 24:20.333
- One carpaccio.
- That's all.

24:31.178 --> 24:32.220
Taiga!

24:33.013 --> 24:34.723
Can you make that order?

24:34.806 --> 24:36.183
Okay.

24:36.266 --> 24:38.143
Here's your omelet.

24:38.226 --> 24:40.103
RIN

24:54.910 --> 24:55.952
Taiga?

25:02.167 --> 25:03.376
Is he mad?

25:07.589 --> 25:10.008
SORRY FOR MAKING YOU WAIT
YOU CAN COME OVER NOW

25:10.091 --> 25:12.344
WHERE ARE YOU?

25:15.055 --> 25:16.806
You promised…

25:35.784 --> 25:37.202
- Excuse me!
- Yes!

25:55.220 --> 25:56.346
LEE YUNGYEOL: HAPPY BIRTHDAY!
MIZUKI: RIN - HAPPY BIRTHDAY!

25:56.429 --> 25:57.472
JUNHO: HAPPY BIRTHDAY!

25:57.555 --> 25:58.473
LEE HAEUN: HAPPY BIRTHDAY, RIN!
TODAY IS YOUR DAY!

25:58.556 --> 25:59.724
MAMAMON: HAPPY BIRTHDAY, MY GIRL!
I'LL LOVE YOU FOREVER!

25:59.808 --> 26:01.101
YUN CHAEWON: IT'S YOUR BIRTHDAY! WOW!
WHEN WILL WE HAVE THE PARTY?

26:01.601 --> 26:02.727
TAIGA

26:02.811 --> 26:04.312
SORRY FOR MAKING YOU WAIT
YOU CAN COME OVER NOW

26:04.396 --> 26:05.689
WHERE ARE YOU?

26:06.940 --> 26:08.108
Why?

26:22.247 --> 26:24.040
Unbelievable!

26:24.791 --> 26:26.584
- Thanks.
- Thank you.

26:26.668 --> 26:28.086
Thank you.

26:31.298 --> 26:33.550
Finally, they're gone.

26:35.760 --> 26:36.928
Thanks so much for today.

26:37.012 --> 26:38.471
- You really saved me.
- No worries.

26:44.352 --> 26:45.812
RIN

26:46.521 --> 26:48.148
Oh crap!

26:54.154 --> 26:55.363
TAIGA

26:58.700 --> 27:01.119
TOMORROW - I'LL GO
FIRST THING IN THE MORNING

27:38.323 --> 27:39.699
Happy birthday!

27:50.877 --> 27:52.837
Why didn't you say anything?

27:53.713 --> 27:54.631
What?

27:56.257 --> 27:57.884
I was waiting for you the whole time.

27:58.635 --> 28:01.888
I messaged you as soon as eomma left.
I was looking forward to it!

28:02.680 --> 28:03.765
Sorry.

28:05.558 --> 28:07.310
I noticed around midnight

28:08.353 --> 28:09.979
and called you right away…

28:11.231 --> 28:13.608
Why didn't you
check your phone until then?

28:15.110 --> 28:16.861
I was busy at work.

28:16.945 --> 28:18.947
What? You said you had the day off.

28:19.030 --> 28:20.031
Well…

28:20.949 --> 28:22.826
I was asked to work that evening.

28:24.411 --> 28:27.580
Tell me those kinds of things.
Why didn't you say anything?

28:27.664 --> 28:28.998
That's because…

28:32.335 --> 28:34.879
I thought you were having fun
with your mom.

28:38.967 --> 28:40.927
I'm sorry about eomma coming…

28:42.971 --> 28:47.642
But I wanted to be with you
when it became my birthday.

28:51.020 --> 28:53.648
When you like someone,
don't you naturally want to talk to them?

28:54.190 --> 28:56.568
Not just once a day,
or because you have to.

28:57.318 --> 29:00.155
- You can't even put in that effort for me.
- Wait.

29:01.573 --> 29:03.908
I'm sorry for not telling you.

29:04.951 --> 29:07.495
- But that has nothing to do with--
- It does!

29:08.163 --> 29:10.832
I like to hear from you.

29:10.915 --> 29:13.168
And when you put in the effort,
it makes me happy.

29:14.502 --> 29:15.503
Why don't you get that?

29:25.138 --> 29:29.225
All my friends from Korea
contacted me at midnight.

29:30.560 --> 29:34.105
That is how important
birthdays are to them.

29:38.109 --> 29:39.819
How was I supposed to know…

29:42.572 --> 29:44.908
Don't push your standards on me.

29:55.043 --> 29:57.545
Fine. Whatever.

30:54.018 --> 30:57.438
Here's your water.

30:58.398 --> 31:00.149
TANOMI

31:00.233 --> 31:01.651
Hello.

31:01.734 --> 31:03.069
Oh, what's wrong?

31:03.152 --> 31:06.406
Plans have changed, so can I work today?

31:06.489 --> 31:07.532
Changed?

31:08.658 --> 31:10.702
I see…

31:10.785 --> 31:13.288
Sorry, that was my fault.

31:13.371 --> 31:15.874
No, it's not your fault, Shige.

31:18.376 --> 31:20.461
Maybe it is difficult for two people

31:21.045 --> 31:23.214
from different backgrounds to be together?

31:26.092 --> 31:28.803
You two are separate human beings,
so running into problems

31:28.887 --> 31:30.430
is to be expected.

31:31.389 --> 31:33.975
It's not convincing,
coming from a single guy, huh?

31:38.062 --> 31:40.064
What do you think was the problem?

31:44.944 --> 31:48.031
I can't seem to keep up with her.

31:49.157 --> 31:50.909
She wants to communicate regularly,

31:50.992 --> 31:52.952
but I don't understand that concept.

31:53.703 --> 31:56.915
Of course, it can't be helped
that we're from different cultures.

31:56.998 --> 31:59.459
And I thought
that it wouldn't matter, but…

32:01.377 --> 32:04.047
Why did Rin say that she wants
to communicate regularly?

32:06.299 --> 32:07.592
She said…

32:08.635 --> 32:11.679
she wants me to know more about her.

32:15.558 --> 32:19.228
Then I don't think it's the lack
of communication that she's mad about.

32:25.026 --> 32:28.029
It's okay to run into problems.

32:44.379 --> 32:45.338
Shige.

32:46.339 --> 32:48.549
Can I take today off, after all?

32:49.384 --> 32:51.511
Sure. Good luck.

34:01.581 --> 34:02.457
Rin.

34:03.332 --> 34:04.375
Taiga…

34:10.590 --> 34:11.883
Hey, wait!

34:13.426 --> 34:14.469
Rin!

34:48.628 --> 34:49.670
I'm sorry…

34:52.924 --> 34:56.969
I couldn't celebrate
your birthday with you.

34:59.889 --> 35:04.310
If I had communicated with you,
this wouldn't have happened.

35:30.628 --> 35:33.589
I'm sorry too.

35:34.799 --> 35:36.884
I was only thinking about myself.

35:38.052 --> 35:40.138
I wasn't thinking about your feelings.

35:49.397 --> 35:50.898
Your present…

35:50.982 --> 35:52.150
I loved it.

35:53.401 --> 35:55.319
I barely told you about it…

35:55.862 --> 35:57.488
But you remembered?

36:00.241 --> 36:04.078
When you said that you're a big fan,
your eyes were sparkling.

36:05.288 --> 36:07.123
I could tell you really liked it.

36:08.833 --> 36:11.878
You were trying
to get to know me, after all.

36:18.634 --> 36:19.886
Lately,

36:21.220 --> 36:22.597
when I'm cooking,

36:23.681 --> 36:25.558
I think of you.

36:29.103 --> 36:31.439
"Will she like this,
if I make this for her?"

36:32.899 --> 36:36.736
"What would she say
if I sent a photo of this to her?"

36:39.739 --> 36:41.073
I should have

36:43.409 --> 36:44.744
told you all these things.

36:47.413 --> 36:50.333
We can talk to each other any time.
We're dating, after all.

37:04.263 --> 37:05.223
From now on…

37:07.516 --> 37:09.560
I want to know more about

37:10.895 --> 37:12.188
the things you value.

37:15.691 --> 37:16.859
Thank you.

37:19.403 --> 37:20.446
Me too.

38:33.602 --> 38:35.521
Welcome home, Taiga.

38:35.604 --> 38:37.940
Don't get the wrong idea.
Anyone can do that.

38:38.024 --> 38:41.193
I wasn't able to live up to my
family's expectations.

38:41.277 --> 38:42.945
I don't think so!

38:43.029 --> 38:43.904
Subtitle translation by: Kiko Morita
